{
  "slug": "wiki-knowledge-complier",
  "name": "Wiki Knowledge Complier",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "A. wiki-knowledge-compiler turns Claude Code into an AI-powered knowledge management system that:\n\nB. Workflow\nIngest → Compile → Link → Query → Write-back → Improve\n\nEach interaction improves your knowledge base over time - turning answers into reusable assets instead of one-off responses.\n\n- Ingests raw sources (PDFs, markdown, notes, URL stubs) into an immutable archive.\n- Extracts atomic concepts, creates summaries, and builds topic pages — all with provenance.\n- Queries the knowledge base with citations and writes back reusable answers.\n- Maintains structural health: detects orphans, duplicates, stale pages, and broken links.\n- Synthesizes cross-cutting insights with explicit confidence ratings and uncertainty markers.\n- Everything is plain markdown with YAML frontmatter. No databases, no cloud services, no proprietary formats.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **4 agents** and **7 commands**.\n\n- **Agents** (4): `wiki-auditor` (Specialized agent for auditing the structural health of the knowledge base — finds orphans, duplicates, stale content, broken…), `wiki-ingestor` (Specialized agent for ingesting raw sources into the knowledge base), `wiki-librarian` (Specialized agent for searching, navigating, and answering questions from the knowledge base), `wiki-synthesizer` (Specialized agent for generating cross-cutting insights, identifying patterns, and discovering knowledge gaps across the knowledge base)\n- **Commands** (7): `wiki-audit` (Check wiki health — find broken links, stale content, contradictions, and auto-fix what it can), `wiki-ingest` (Add a document to your wiki — creates summaries, extracts key ideas, and connects everything), `wiki-insights` (Discover connections and patterns across your sources), `wiki-schedule` (Schedule /wiki-update to run automatically — by time, interval, or both), `wiki-setup` (Set up your wiki — choose your project size and get started), `wiki-update` (Sync your wiki — ingest new files in raw/ and refresh indexes), `wiki` (Ask a question — get an answer from your wiki with sources)\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install wiki-knowledge-complier@claude-community` from `bradduy/wiki-knowledge-compiler`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "agent": 4,
    "command": 7
  },
